  "analysis": [
    {
      "label": "Context",
      "text": "The Czechs led 1–0 and Scotland were pushing bodies forward, with the goalkeeper high up to sweep behind a back line playing well away from goal."
    },
    {
      "label": "The turnover",
      "text": "Scotland tried to build through midfield, but the clearing header went back into their own half. The ball dropped to Schick around the halfway line with the pitch open ahead."
    },
    {
      "label": "The decision",
      "text": "Schick had checked the goalkeeper's position while the ball was still travelling. Marshall was several metres off the line, which made the goal a bigger target than the distance suggested."
    },
    {
      "label": "The strike",
      "text": "One touch to set it, then struck with the laces and lifted early. The ball climbed quickly, cleared the retreating keeper and dropped inside the far post from 45 metres."
    }
  ],
  "lessons": [
    {
      "label": "Look before it arrives",
      "text": "Schick checks the keeper's position while the ball is still in the air. Deciding after the touch would have been a second too late."
    },
    {
      "label": "Lift it early",
      "text": "A long lob has to climb fast to clear a sprinting keeper. Lean back slightly and strike under the middle of the ball."
    },
    {
      "label": "Aim across, not straight",
      "text": "Sending it towards the far post gives the keeper the longest possible recovery run, and leaves room for the ball to drop inside the post."
    },
    {
      "label": "Keepers: mind the line",
      "text": "Sweeping high up the pitch is useful until the ball turns over. When possession flips, the first job is getting back."
    }
  ],
  "note": "The ball's path, its timing and the tracked players come from StatsBomb's open data for this match (id 3788748). Players the data only sees at the shot have routes drawn back into those positions, and any extra team-mates are placed by hand. Commentary is original, not the broadcast."
